em for convex bodies with given area measure.\nTitle: Hölder continuity for support measures of convex bodies\nAuthors: Daniel Hug, Rolf Schneider\nDate: Sun Jan 25 21:59:45 2015\n\nThe support measures of a convex body are a common generalization of the curvature measures and the area measures. With respect to the Hausdorff metric on the space of convex bodies, they are weakly continuous. We provide a quantitative improvement of this result, by establishing a H\\\"older estimate for the support measures in terms of the bounded Lipschitz metric, which metrizes the weak convergence. Specializing the result to area measures yields a reverse counterpart to earlier stability estimates, concerning Minkowski's existence theorem for convex bodies with given area measure.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHölder continuity of normal cycles and of support measures of convex bodies (https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1514)\nciteturn1academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.0 years ago; Title: Hölder continuity of normal cycles and of support measures of convex bodiesAuthors: Daniel Hug, Rolf Schneider ... We also give an estimate (in the bounded Lipschitz metric) of the support measures of convex bodies.\nTitle: Hölder continuity of normal cycles and of support measures of convex bodies\nAuthors: Daniel Hug, Rolf Schneider\nDate: Sat Oct  5 20:07:29 2013\n\nWe provide an estimate of the distance (in the dual flat seminorm) of the normal cycles of convex bodies with given Hausdorff distance. We also give an estimate (in the bounded Lipschitz metric) of the support measures of convex bodies.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAround Bezout inequalities for mixed volumes (https://congreso.us.es/convie/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/szusterman.pdf)\nciteturn1search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; The inradius of K relative to L is ... ▶A corollary of Diskant’s inequality : ... for any 